.TH DCANCEL 8 "2026-10-26"
.SH NAME
dcancel \- Diablo program to cancel articles by hand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcancel
.B \-a
|
.B \-h
|
.B \-s
|
.B \-r
[
.B \-u
]
[
.B \-n
]
[
.BR \-v [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.B \-V
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dcancel
cancels articles listed on standard input, one per line, without a cancel
control message.  At least one of
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-h ,
.B \-s
or
.B \-r
is required.  For
.BR \-a ,
.B \-h
and
.B \-s
each line holds a Message-ID; for
.B \-r
each line holds
.IR group : number .
Leading blanks are ignored, and anything after the first blank is ignored.
.PP
.B \-h
marks the article's entry in the feeder's dhistory as expired, so the
feeder no longer serves it and refuses it if it is offered again.
.B \-s
removes the article from the spool: every spool file that holds a
cancelled article is rewritten without it (an emptied file is removed),
and the history entry is updated to the new location.  Rewriting spool
files while diablo is writing to them is not recommended.
.B \-a
does both, and is the normal way to cancel on a feeder.
.PP
.B \-r
cancels the article in the reader's overview (header index) for the
group, so dreaderd no longer lists or serves it there.  It does not touch
the feeder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Cancel in the history and the spool (\fB\-h\fP and \fB\-s\fP).
.TP
.B \-h
Cancel in the history only.
.TP
.B \-s
Cancel in the spool only.
.TP
.B \-r
Cancel in the reader overview; input lines are \fIgroup\fP:\fInumber\fP.
.TP
.B \-u
Uncancel: clear the expired mark of the history entries instead
(with \fB\-h\fP).
.TP
.B \-n
Report what would be cancelled ("Would cancel ...") without changing
the history or the spool.
.TP
.BR \-v [\fIn\fP]
Be more verbose, optionally with a level.
.TP
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
Set the debug level.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
echo '<abc@example.com>' | dcancel -a -v
echo 'misc.test:1234' | dcancel -r
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diablo(8),
dreaderd(8),
dhisctl(8),
dexpire(8),
dexpireover(8),
diablo-files(5)
